ok   a GET over h2c is answered with the status, the default headers and the body
ok   the request carries HTTP/2, its method, :authority as Host and its query
ok   several requests on one connection, and a body in several DATA frames
ok   interleaved streams are answered in the order their requests became whole
ok   a body larger than the window is sent as the client opens it
ok   a client window of 0 holds the body until WINDOW_UPDATE
ok   a response header block past the frame size goes out in CONTINUATION
ok   a request header block in HEADERS and CONTINUATION is read whole
ok   HEAD and 304 have headers and no DATA
ok   cookies are joined with '; ', set-cookie is one field each, connection-specific fields are dropped
ok   values are trimmed, te is dropped, and non-ASCII values and bodies are sent as bytes
ok   trailers end a request
ok   a padded DATA and a padded, prioritized HEADERS are read
ok   an exception is a 500, a client fault a 400, and the connection stays
ok   a content-length over max_body_bytes is 413 and the stream is reset
ok   a header list over max_head_bytes is 400
ok   malformed requests are reset with PROTOCOL_ERROR
ok   streams past max_streams are refused
ok   a stream the client resets before its turn is not answered
ok   a first frame that is not SETTINGS is a PROTOCOL_ERROR
ok   DATA on stream 0, PUSH_PROMISE and an even stream are PROTOCOL_ERRORs
ok   a header block interrupted by another frame is a PROTOCOL_ERROR
ok   a broken header block is a COMPRESSION_ERROR
ok   a frame over the frame size and a bad PING are FRAME_SIZE_ERRORs
ok   a header block past max_head_bytes compressed ends the connection
ok   a WINDOW_UPDATE past 2^31-1 on the connection is a FLOW_CONTROL_ERROR
ok   PING is answered with its payload, and SETTINGS with an ACK
ok   an idle connection gets GOAWAY after read_timeout
ok   a body not whole within body_timeout is 408
ok   stop sends GOAWAY to an idle connection, answers the request in flight, and drains
ok   a BodyWriter streams DATA frames and ends the stream; the connection stays
ok   a writer's wait_closed sees the client reset its stream
ok   HTTP/1.1 is served as before on a server with http2
ok   with http2: false the preface is a 400
34 tests, 122 assertions, 0 failures
